From: Altium-on-Wine kit
Subject: winhttp: don't cap the response-header wait for apps that set an infinite receive timeout

Modules: dlls/winhttp
Base: wine-11.16

When an app doesn't set WINHTTP_OPTION_RECEIVE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT, Wine waits only 21 s for
response headers. libgit2 (1.7.1 in Altium 26's Git extension) calls
WinHttpSetTimeouts(request, -1, 60000, -1, -1) and nothing else, and Altium 365's Git
server can take longer than 21 s to answer a git-upload-pack POST, so cloning a project
failed with "failed to receive response". Requests whose receive timeout is infinite now
wait for headers without a cap; everything else keeps Wine's 21 s default.

Tested with a local server that delays headers 25 s: stock fails (error 10060) at 21.0 s,
patched returns 200 at 25.0 s. winhttp notification tests are unchanged.

--- a/dlls/winhttp/request.c
+++ b/dlls/winhttp/request.c
@@ -2008,7 +2008,16 @@
 
 static int get_receive_response_timeout( struct request *request )
 {
-    if (request->receive_response_timeout == -1) return ACTUAL_DEFAULT_RECEIVE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT;
+    if (request->receive_response_timeout == -1)
+    {
+        /* Altium-on-Wine kit: an app that asked for an infinite receive timeout (e.g. libgit2,
+         * which calls WinHttpSetTimeouts( h, -1, 60000, -1, -1 )) gets no 21 s cap on the wait
+         * for response headers either. Altium 365's Git server can take longer than that to
+         * answer a git-upload-pack POST, and the clone then failed with "failed to receive
+         * response". Other apps keep Wine's default. */
+        if (!request->receive_timeout) return 0;
+        return ACTUAL_DEFAULT_RECEIVE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT;
+    }
     return request->receive_response_timeout;
 }
 
